---
import SectionBar from './SectionBar.astro';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
const areas = [
  { name: 'Static analysis', text: 'Reading what a program declares before running it. Android manifest permissions and intent actions feed a classifier, and the APK is never executed.', href: '#p-android', evidence: 'Android Malware Detection' },
  { name: 'Binary reversing', text: 'Ghidra-based disassembly and decompilation, practiced on reverse-engineering and binary challenges in CTFs: recovering behavior from machine code.', href: '#ctf', evidence: 'CTF log' },
  { name: 'Malware triage', text: 'A static-first screening pass with explainable risk indicators, and an honest account of what static analysis misses: obfuscation and dynamic payloads.', href: '#p-android', evidence: 'Detector limitations' },
  { name: 'Protocol and traffic analysis', text: 'Verifying behavior at packet level: ESP on the WAN side against RDP on the LAN side in Wireshark, and flow debugging a tunnel that negotiated but dropped return traffic.', href: '#p-forti', evidence: 'FortiGate VPN & HA Lab' },
];
---
<section id="research" class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="research-title">
  <SectionBar label="Reverse engineering / security" addr="00401020" />
  <h2 id="research-title">Understanding software below the source.</h2>
  <p class="sec-intro">The common thread in my work is recovering behavior from artifacts: manifests, packets, binaries, and logs.</p>
  <div class="focus-grid">
    <ul class="focus-list">
      {areas.map(a => (
        <li>
          <h3>{a.name}</h3>
          <p>{a.text}</p>
          <a class="evidence" href={a.href}><span class="xref" aria-hidden="true">; xref</span>{a.evidence} <Icon /></a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <aside class="writeups-note" aria-labelledby="writeups-title">
      <div>
        <p class="label">Research / writeups</p>
        <h3 id="writeups-title">Coming as I publish analyses.</h3>
      </div>
      <p>No reversing writeups are published yet. The site is ready for them, and each will carry the material that makes an analysis checkable:</p>
      <ul aria-label="Planned writeup contents"><li>disassembly</li><li>pseudocode</li><li>call graphs</li><li>hexdumps</li><li>strings</li><li>method notes</li></ul>
      <p class="hexline" aria-hidden="true"><span class="hx">00000000</span>  7f 45 4c 46  <span>|.ELF|</span></p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>
